WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
A tumor can enlarge without yet establishing a distant

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.006
deposit.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:06.070
First examine its boundary with surrounding tissue.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.617
Watch protease activity open
a path through extracellular matrix

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.940
and basement membrane.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:15.753
Reduced adhesion and increased
migration help cells leave the

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.480
original site.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.207
Entry into blood or lymph is not enough.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.340
Cells must survive transport and grow in a receptive

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:23.364
distant environment.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.356
Local invasion and successful
metastasis are separate steps.
